  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs#impl[UnreadContents/NodeContents]/fn[format]` is sound.\n\n- **Form:** The justification is fenced `{cite}` commentary on an explicit function with a body, and it gives a substantive reason for the exception. `format` is `match *self {}` on `UnreadContents`, which is an empty enum (`pub enum UnreadContents {}`). No value of that type can exist, so the body can never run. The coverage gap is therefore a real impossibility, not just difficulty.\n- **Agreement with current source:** The commentary says storage tests supply no content values and reject node reads at the domain boundary. That matches `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]`. It returns `Result<UnreadContents, _>` but panics with \"storage operations must not read graph contents\". `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/type[NodeContent]` sets `NodeContent = UnreadContents`, so the trait impl is needed only to satisfy the associated-type bound.\n- **Role:** The citation is a built-in, and it is the only reference on this item. No `{impl}` or `{test}` is also present, so nothing is redundant.",
